bottleneck.py at ResNet50's ACTUAL conv2_x shape (56x56) -- the shape every prior
measurement in this project could not reach, now unblocked by two fixes:
  1. conv2dk3 / conv2dk1 / conv2dk1_skip's width-32-only kernel restriction
     (results/aie/conv2dk3_widthfix_npu.log, results/aie/bottleneck_widthfix_npu.log)
  2. Tile(0,4)'s L1 budget: single-buffered the final output ObjectFifo (depth=1
     instead of the default 2) in the local mlir-aie checkout's bottleneck.py --
     the one buffer of Tile(0,4)'s five that is safe to shrink without touching the
     skip connection's timing. See the patch comment in bottleneck.py itself.
Desktop 2 (Ryzen 7 8700G / Phoenix XDNA1), 2026-09-07, both sides one sitting.

  NPU : kernels/bottleneck_sweep/sweep.py --shapes 32x56,56x56 --iters 5 --warmup 1
  CPU : kernels/bottleneck_sweep/cpu_sweep.py --shapes 32x56,56x56 --iters 100 --warmup 10

CORRECTNESS
===========
Both NPU shapes verified against the torch int8 golden before timing (sweep.py's
existing gate, DataShaper YCXC8/CYX in, OIYXI8O8/OIYX weights, CDYX/YCXD out).
32x56: ok=yes. 56x56: ok=yes.

